&#8220;I liked her, nice kid,&#8221; the actor began. &#8220;She was very professional. She&#8217;s terrific and very quick and got it all. She was very much part of the whole process.&#8221;

De Niro was previously familiar with Grande&#8217;s acting through his daughter, who was a big fan of Nickelodeon&#8217;s Victorious while growing up.

&#8220;I had seen her in some stuff with my daughter, some sitcom thing she had done. I&#8217;m forgetting the name,&#8221; he said. &#8220;My kid was into that. I was aware of her then and, of course, aware of her in other ways. She was great.&#8221;

The Academy Award winner still hasn&#8217;t seen Grande&#8217;s performance in Wicked , but plans to do so in the near future.

&#8220;I didn&#8217;t see her movie, and I still am trying to see it, believe it or not, but I want to see it,&#8221; he added. &#8220;I&#8217;m going to see it with my daughter. And she&#8217;s, of course, seen it.&#8221;

While a film&#8217;s cast is made up of actors coming from different disciplines and schools of thought, De Niro preached the importance of making sure everyone&#8217;s on the same page on set.

&#8220;It&#8217;s really so important that everybody sort of gets it and jumps in quick, and the timing and the give-and-take is there,&#8221; he said. &#8220;Everybody understands what we&#8217;re doing. It&#8217;s all very professional. It really helps.&#8221;

When Billboard interviewed De Niro last month, the actor joked of Grande: &#8220;She sings my character a lot of songs. No, she was great. Everybody was very happy she was going to do it.&#8221;

Focker-in-Law serves as the fourth installment of the Meet the Parents film series, as the original arrived in 2000. Focker-in-Law hits theaters on Nov. 25.

A trailer for the Universal blockbuster arrived in April, which found De Niro testing Ariana Grande (Olivia Jones) with his lie detector machine. Grande dates Ben Stiller&#8217;s (Gaylord Focker) son in the movie, who&#8217;s played by Skyler Gisondo. Stiller doesn&#8217;t trust Grande and he&#8217;s hesitant to let his son tie the knot with her.

Robert De Niro reprises his role as Jack Byrnes, and he seems to be a much bigger fan of Grande than he was of Stiller in the previous films from the series.

On the music side, Grande released her Petal lead single &#8220;Hate That I Made You Love Me&#8221; on May 29. Petal is set to arrive on July 31. The LP is Grande&#8217;s eighth and serves as the follow-up to Eternal Sunshine , which topped the Billboard 200 in 2024.

